# 🚀 ORBITAL: Mission Control — Developer Setup & Run Guide

This single-file developer guide covers everything needed to clone, install, configure, migrate the local database, and run the **ORBITAL: Mission Control** monorepo on your local machine.

---

## 📋 1. Prerequisites

Ensure you have the following installed on your development workstation:

| Tool | Minimum Version | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Node.js** | `v22+` (v26 verified) | Node runtime (`node -v`) |
| **pnpm** | `v10+` (v12 verified) | Package manager (`npm install -g pnpm`) |
| **Git** | Latest stable | Version control (`git --version`) |
| **Browser** | Latest Chrome / Edge / Firefox | WebGL 2.0 support for 3D Earth & Satellite canvas |

> **Note on Database:** You **do NOT need Docker or external PostgreSQL installed**. ORBITAL uses **PGlite** (an embedded WebAssembly/C PostgreSQL engine) for local development.

---

## ⚡ 2. Quickstart (Under 2 Minutes)

Open PowerShell or terminal in your repository directory:

```powershell
# 1. Install all dependencies across all apps and packages
pnpm install

# 2. Setup environment variables (copy templates if not already present)
Copy-Item apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
Copy-Item apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env.local -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue

# 3. Initialize the local PGlite database, run migrations, and load seed scenarios
pnpm db:setup

# 4. Start both Frontend and Backend concurrently
pnpm dev
```

---

## 🌐 3. Local Services & URLs

Once `pnpm dev` is running, open the following URLs in your browser:

| Service | Local URL | Description |
|---|---|---|
| **Frontend Web App** | [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) | Interactive 3D Mission Control browser game |
| **Backend API** | [http://localhost:4000](http://localhost:4000) | Express REST API & Socket.IO multiplayer server |
| **API Health Check** | [http://localhost:4000/health](http://localhost:4000/health) | Returns JSON status and database connectivity |

---

## ⚙️ 4. Environment Configuration

The monorepo provides `.env.example` templates for both frontend and backend.

### Backend (`apps/api/.env`)
```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
CLIENT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
DATABASE_PROVIDER=pglite
PGLITE_DATA_DIR=.local/pglite
```

### Frontend (`apps/web/.env.local`)
```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
VITE_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:4000
```

> **Security Rule:** Never prefix backend database connection strings or secrets with `VITE_`.

---

## 🗄️ 5. Database Management (PGlite & Drizzle ORM)

Local database files are stored inside `apps/api/.local/pglite/`.

### Available Database Commands:

```powershell
# Complete initialization (migrations + seed scenarios)
pnpm db:setup

# Apply schema migrations to local database
pnpm db:migrate

# Populate/refresh mission scenario seed data
pnpm db:seed

# Generate new migration files after modifying packages/database/src/schema.ts
pnpm db:generate

# Hard reset: drops all tables, applies migrations, and re-seeds (non-destructive to Git)
pnpm db:reset
```

### Database Tables:
- `missions`: Preloaded scientific scenarios (Earth Sentinel, Artemis, Ares, NEA).
- `spacecraft_designs`: Saved modular spacecraft configurations and telemetry snapshots.
- `launch_configs`: Validated booster and trajectory pairing records.
- `mission_rooms`: Active multiplayer room states and codes.
- `team_members`: Connected engineers, assigned roles, and readiness status.
- `mission_reports`: Historical post-flight evaluation scores and accolades.

---

## 🏃 6. Running Services Independently

You can run individual services if you are working exclusively on one module:

```powershell
# Run ONLY Frontend (Vite on port 5173)
pnpm --filter @orbital/web dev

# Run ONLY Backend API & Sockets (Express on port 4000)
pnpm --filter @orbital/api dev

# Run ONLY Database package scripts
pnpm --filter @orbital/database db:setup
```

---

## 🧪 7. Quality Checks, Testing & Building

Before committing or opening a PR, run the automated verification suite:

```powershell
# 1. Type check all 6 workspace packages and apps
pnpm typecheck

# 2. Run unit tests (Astrodynamics, vis-viva, power balance, crisis resolution)
pnpm test

# 3. Build production bundles for all packages and web apps
pnpm build
```

---

## 📂 8. Monorepo Project Structure

```text
orbital-mission-control/
├── apps/
│   ├── web/                    # React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Three.js (R3F), Zustand
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── features/       # 5 Core Game Feature Modules:
│   │   │   │   ├── mission-hub/          # M01: Scenarios & briefings
│   │   │   │   ├── spacecraft-lab/       # M02: Modular spacecraft builder & 3D visualizer
│   │   │   │   ├── orbit-launch/         # M03: 3D Earth trajectory & booster selector
│   │   │   │   ├── mission-operations/   # M04: Telemetry monitors, crises & reports
│   │   │   │   └── multiplayer/          # M05: Room lobby, roles & tactical chat
│   │   │   ├── three/                    # 3D R3F Canvas components (SpacecraftCanvas, EarthOrbitCanvas)
│   │   │   └── store/                    # Zustand centralized game store
│   │
│   └── api/                    # Node.js, Express, Socket.IO, Drizzle ORM
│       └── src/
│           ├── routes/         # REST endpoints (/health, /api/scenarios, /api/designs, etc.)
│           └── sockets/        # Real-time room sync, telemetry tick loop & crisis events
│
├── packages/
│   ├── contracts/              # Shared Zod validation schemas & TypeScript types
│   ├── simulation-engine/      # Orbital mechanics, power margin calculations & tick simulator
│   ├── game-data/              # Catalogs: scenarios, components, orbits, vehicles, crises
│   └── database/               # Drizzle ORM schema, PGlite client, migration & seed scripts
│
├── database/
│   ├── migrations/             # SQL DDL migrations
│   └── seeds/                  # Scenarios JSON seed files
│
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml
├── tsconfig.base.json
├── package.json
└── README.dev                  # This file
```

