## 🔧 9. Troubleshooting

### 1. `node` or `pnpm` not recognized in PowerShell
Ensure Node.js and pnpm paths are loaded in your current shell session:
```powershell
$env:PATH = "C:\Program Files\nodejs;C:\Program Files\Git\cmd;C:\Users\$env:USERNAME\AppData\Roaming\npm;" + $env:PATH
```

### 2. Port `5173` or `4000` is already in use
Check what process is holding the port and terminate it:
```powershell
Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 4000, 5173 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object OwningProcess, LocalPort
Stop-Process -Id <PID> -Force
```

### 3. Local PGlite database is inconsistent or locked
Reset the local embedded database back to clean state:
```powershell
pnpm db:reset
```

### 4. Multiplayer Socket fails to connect
- Verify that `apps/api` is running on port 4000 (`http://localhost:4000/health`).
- Ensure `VITE_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:4000` is present in `apps/web/.env.local`.

---

## 👥 10. Five Developer Feature Module Ownership

| Module | Module Name | Primary Responsibilities |
|---|---|---|
| **M01** | **Mission Hub** | Scientific campaigns, briefings, hazard requirements & difficulty ratings |
| **M02** | **Spacecraft Lab** | 3D satellite assembly, mass/power/budget telemetry & validation rules |
| **M03** | **Orbit & Launch** | 3D Earth globe, trajectory ellipses, vis-viva math & rocket compatibility |
| **M04** | **Operations Center** | Real-time flight clock, telemetry streaming, crisis choices & debrief reports |
| **M05** | **Multiplayer** | Socket.IO rooms, 4 engineering roles (Flight Dir, Systems, Trajectory, Science) & chat |

